  "slug": "recovery-model-2949",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications introduce metrics that score whether embeddings and structural descriptors faithfully retain their source geometry.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of explicit, quantitative criteria to judge whether a derived representation faithfully reflects the structure of its source data. velotest applies a cell-level statistical test to RNA velocity embeddings and reports embedding quality differences that bear on trajectory visualization. MDQ adapts DockQ-style scoring into a symmetric, reference-free comparison of protein-protein interfaces across molecular dynamics frames, yielding a distance metric for clustering. OT-tSNE addresses batch integration in visualization by replacing cross-batch nearest-neighbour matching with entropic optimal-transport affinities. CNR contributes a structure-derived atlas of density- and topology-corrected response descriptors for 22,167 human proteins. What is new across these items is the packaging of such criteria as scored, reproducible metrics. The works are heterogeneous in scope, and this thread describes the common emphasis rather than a shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
